Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Register .q language + e2e extraction pipeline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

T14: register the KDB+/q extractor across graphify's wiring:
- extract.py: import extract_q, add .q -> extract_q in _DISPATCH
- extractors/__init__.py: LANGUAGE_EXTRACTORS['q'] = extract_q
- detect.py: add .q to CODE_EXTENSIONS (watch.py derives from it)
- pyproject.toml: [project.optional-dependencies] q = ['tree-sitter-q']

T15: end-to-end test through the real dispatch (_get_extractor) on a golden
.q file — asserts functions, a call edge, namespace-qualified names, an
import edge, and a table 'uses' edge, and passes validate_extraction.

extractor fix: walk the whole lambda for calls/qsql instead of
child_by_field_name('body') — a multi-statement body tags every statement
with the body field and child_by_field_name returned only the first, missing
calls/qsql in later statements (e.g. select inside {a:1; select from t}).

All 12 q extractor tests pass.
